  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Malaria Elimination Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry Americas EMMIE - Malaria - Inter-American Development Bank - IDB.  This program has the following goals: To achieve sustainable malaria elimination in Belize, Costa Rica, the Dominican Republic, El Salvador, Guatemala, Honduras, Nicaragua, and Panama by 2020. The objectives of this program are: To create a positive demonstration effect of innovative financing for malaria elimination in other geographic areas or for other diseases in Central America.  To  strengthen the policy environmnet for malaria elimination updating national regulations and policies with evidence on new strategies and tools for malaria elimination and prevention of re-emergence in 8 Host Countries by year 5..  To contribute to increase domestic funding included in national budgets for malaria elimination and re-emergence prevention in 8 Host Countries by year 5 through IDB loans and financial incentives to be provided through a &apos;results based funding modality&apos;..  To improve the planning processes and operations at national level improving the quality of health systems,  case management, vector control and logistics for malaria elimination in Host Countries by year 5..  To strengthen surveillance systems and data quality for malaria elimination in 8 Host Countries by year 3.  To facilitate collective impact by aligning  country and partner financial and technical resources according to Host Country needs</narrative>
  </description>
